 "id": "01a10795-e961-7b32-b444-2651b9fc2159",
 "content": "scripts/export.py produces the monthly invoice report that Finance imports into their accounting tool at the start of each month. It runs from the ops cron on the 2nd at 06:00 UTC and writes one file per environment to EXPORT_BUCKET under `exports/<YYYY-MM>/invoices.csv`. Finance reconciles the totals against the ledger, so every finalized invoice of the month must appear exactly once, including zero-amount ones; drafts are excluded. Columns, in order: invoice id, customer id, subtotal, tax, total, finalized date. Amounts are integer cents with no currency symbol. Format requirements of Finance's import tool (new tool adopted late Sept 2026, replacing the German-locale one that needed `;` and DD.MM.YYYY): plain comma-separated, dates ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` (strftime `%Y-%m-%d`), UTF-8 without a BOM.",
 "summary": "Monthly export: Finance import needs comma-delimited CSV, ISO dates, integer cents, all finalized invoices once",
 "valid_from": "2026-09-27T00:00:00Z"
}
